From: Gilly1970 <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: tolerate reset-asserted RTL8261N on match

rtl826x_probe() loads rtl8261n.bin with request_firmware_direct() and
returns -EPROBE_DEFER while the root filesystem is not mounted yet.
phy_probe() then re-asserts the PHY reset-gpios, so when the deferred
probe is retried rtl8261n_match_phy_device() reads VEND1 PKG_MODEL from
a PHY that is held in reset.

Since "generic: harden RTL826x PHY match, EEE and soft-reset" the match
requires PKG_MODEL == 0x8261. The value read from the reset PHY fails
that test, no driver matches on the retry and phylink attaches the
Generic Clause 45 PHY driver instead. The USXGMII link never comes up.

Seen on the Gemtek W1700K (RTL8261N on lan2 and wan, both with
reset-gpios and 200 ms reset-assert/deassert-us, driver built in).

Go back to rejecting only the known other package models for the
RTL8261N entry. The PHY ID (0x001ccaf3) together with the VERSION_ID
"BE" check already separates it from the RTL8261BE, which keeps the
strict PKG_MODEL test.

Signed-off-by: Gilly1970 <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -3007,7 +3007,8 @@
 	if (data < 0)
 		return 0;
 
-	if (data != RTL826X_VEND1_PKG_MODEL_8261)
+	if (data == RTL826X_VEND1_PKG_MODEL_8251 ||
+	    data == RTL826X_VEND1_PKG_MODEL_8254)
 		return 0;
 
 	data = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND1, RTL826X_VEND1_VERSION_ID);
